</script></head><body><div id="main"><div style="display: none"><a href="/pdfs/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/bedrock-agentcore-dg.pdf#web-search-api-get-started" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Open PDF"></a></div><div id="breadcrumbs" class="breadcrumb"><a href="/index.html">Documentation</a><a href="/bedrock-agentcore/index.html">Amazon Bedrock AgentCore</a><a href="what-is-bedrock-agentcore.html">Developer Guide</a></div><div id="page-toc-src"><a href="#web-search-api-prerequisites">Prerequisites</a><a href="#web-search-api-permissions">Grant permission to call the API</a><a href="#web-search-api-examples">Search the web</a></div><div id="main-content" class="awsui-util-container"><div id="main-col-body"><awsdocs-language-banner data-service="$ctrl.pageService"></awsdocs-language-banner><h1 class="topictitle" id="web-search-api-get-started">Get started with AgentCore Web Search</h1><div class="awsdocs-page-header-container"><awsdocs-page-header></awsdocs-page-header><awsdocs-filter-selector id="awsdocs-filter-selector"></awsdocs-filter-selector></div><p>To search the web with AgentCore Web Search, grant a principal permission to call the <code class="code">InvokeWebSearch</code> API, and then call it with the AWS SDKs or the AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI).</p>
      <h2 id="web-search-api-prerequisites">Prerequisites</h2>
      <p>Before you call the API, make sure that you have the following:</p>
      <div class="itemizedlist">
          
          
          
          
      <ul class="itemizedlist"><li class="listitem">
            <p>An AWS account and credentials that the AWS SDKs or the AWS CLI can use.</p>
         </li><li class="listitem">
            <p>An AWS Region where the API is available. For the list, see <a href="./web-search-api.html#web-search-api-regions">Regions</a>.</p>
         </li><li class="listitem">
            <p>A current version of the AWS SDK for Python (Boto3) or the AWS CLI. Earlier versions don’t include the <code class="code">InvokeWebSearch</code> operation.</p>
         </li><li class="listitem">
            <p>Permission to call the API, as described in the following section.</p>
         </li></ul></div>
    
      <h2 id="web-search-api-permissions">Grant permission to call the API</h2>
      <p>To call the API, an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) principal needs the <code class="code">bedrock-agentcore:InvokeWebSearch</code> permission on the AWS managed web search tool. The tool’s Amazon Resource Name (ARN) has the following form:</p>
      <pre class="programlisting"><div class="code-btn-container"><div class="btn-copy-code" title="Copy"><awsui-icon name="copy"></awsui-icon></div></div><!--DEBUG: cli (text)--><code class="text ">arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:&lt;Region&gt;:aws:tool/web-search.v1</code></pre>
      <p>The account field of the ARN is the literal value <code class="code">aws</code>, because AWS owns the tool. It is not your account ID.</p>
      <p>The following identity-based policy allows a principal to call the API in one Region. Replace <code class="code">&lt;Region&gt;</code> with the code of a Region from <a href="./web-search-api.html#web-search-api-regions">Regions</a>. To allow calls in every Region, use <code class="code">*</code> in place of the Region code.</p>
      <pre class="programlisting"><div class="code-btn-container"><div class="btn-copy-code" title="Copy"><awsui-icon name="copy"></awsui-icon></div></div><!--DEBUG: cli (json)--><code class="json "><span>{</span>
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
        <span>{</span>
            "Sid": "AllowInvokeWebSearch",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": "bedrock-agentcore:InvokeWebSearch",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:&lt;Region&gt;:aws:tool/web-search.v1"
        }
    ]
}</code></pre>
    
      <h2 id="web-search-api-examples">Search the web</h2>
      <p>Only <code class="code">webSearchId</code> and <code class="code">searchQuery</code> are required. The identifier of the AWS managed web search tool is <code class="code">web-search.v1</code>. For an example of the response, see <a href="./web-search-api-reference.html#web-search-api-response">Response</a>.</p>
      <p>The following AWS SDK for Python (Boto3) and AWS CLI examples search for recent pages about a topic. They return up to five results, limit the results to two domains, and keep only pages published in January 2026:</p>
      <div class="example"><h6>Example</h6><div class="example-contents"><awsdocs-tabs><dl style="display: none">
            <dt>
                  AWS SDK (Boto3)</dt><dd tab-id="-------------------aws-sdk-(boto3)">
                  <pre class="programlisting"><div class="code-btn-container"><div class="btn-copy-code" title="Copy"><awsui-icon name="copy"></awsui-icon></div></div><!--DEBUG: cli (python)--><code class="python ">import boto3
from botocore.exceptions import ClientError

client = boto3.client("bedrock-agentcore", region_name="us-east-1")

try:
    response = client.invoke_web_search(
        webSearchId="web-search.v1",
        searchQuery="Amazon Bedrock AgentCore release announcements",
        maxResults=5,
        filters=<span>{</span>
            "domainFilter": <span>{</span>
                "include": ["example.net", "example.org"]
            },
            "publishedDateFilter": <span>{</span>
                "publishedAfter": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                "publishedBefore": "2026-01-31T23:59:59Z"
            }
        }
    )
except ClientError as error:
    print(error.response["Error"]["Code"], error.response["Error"]["Message"])
    raise

for result in response["results"]:
    print(result.get("title"), result.get("url"))
    print(result["text"])</code></pre>
               </dd>
            <dt>
                  AWS CLI</dt><dd tab-id="-------------------aws-cli">
                  <pre class="programlisting"><div class="code-btn-container"><div class="btn-copy-code" title="Copy"><awsui-icon name="copy"></awsui-icon></div></div><!--DEBUG: cli (bash)--><code class="bash ">aws bedrock-agentcore invoke-web-search \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --web-search-id web-search.v1 \
  --search-query "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore release announcements" \
  --max-results 5 \
  --filters '<span>{</span>
    "domainFilter": <span>{</span>"include": ["example.net", "example.org"]},
    "publishedDateFilter": <span>{</span>
      "publishedAfter": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "publishedBefore": "2026-01-31T23:59:59Z"
    }
  }'</code></pre>
               </dd>
         </dl></awsdocs-tabs></div></div>
      <p>For the request fields and their limits, see <a href="./web-search-api-reference.html">Request and response</a>. For the full request and response syntax, see <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/APIReference/API_InvokeWebSearch.html">InvokeWebSearch</a> in the <em>Amazon Bedrock AgentCore API Reference</em>.</p>
